        "original_id": "06537f5f-00f2-54bd-9be7-938f406469a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kelly Preston, John Travolta, Michael B. Druxman, Mark Griffiths, Dan Haggerty, Pato Hoffmann, Michael Angarano, Danielle Panabaker, Kurt Russell, Mary Elizabeth Winstead, Steven Strait, Lynda Carter, Andrew Gunn\n- Films: Cheyenne Warrior, Battlefield Earth, Sky High, Freaky Friday\n- Companies: Walt Disney Pictures\n- Topics: film casts, film production, plot premises\n\nFacts:\n- Cheyenne Warrior is a 1994 American film written by Michael B. Druxman, directed by Mark Griffiths, and starring Kelly Preston, Dan Haggerty, and Pato Hoffmann.\n- Cheyenne Warrior follows a widowed, pregnant woman who is stranded at a trading post during the American Civil War.\n- Kelly Preston is married to John Travolta, and they collaborated on the fantasy film Battlefield Earth.\n- Sky High stars Michael Angarano as Will, Danielle Panabaker as his best friend and love interest, Kurt Russell and Kelly Preston as his parents, Mary Elizabeth Winstead as a popular senior, Steven Strait as Will's rival, and Lynda Carter as Principal Powers.\n- Andrew Gunn worked with Walt Disney Pictures to produce films including Freaky Friday and Sky High.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d1c8f66d-3a8e-52f1-b046-3c80c8480844",
        "text": "Page: Cheyenne Warrior. Sentence: Cheyenne Warrior is a 1994 American film written by Michael B. Druxman, directed by Mark Griffiths, and stars Kelly Preston, Dan Haggerty and Pato Hoffmann.\nPage: Cheyenne Warrior. Sentence: The film follows the struggle of a widowed, pregnant woman who is stranded at a trading post during the American Civil War.\nPage: Kelly Preston. Sentence: She is married to John Travolta, with whom she collaborated on the fantasy film \"Battlefield Earth\".\nPage: Sky High (2005 film). Sentence: The film stars Michael Angarano as Will, an incoming freshman at the school, Danielle Panabaker as his best friend and love interest, Kurt Russell and Kelly Preston as his parents, Mary Elizabeth Winstead as a popular senior, Steven Strait as Will's rival, and Lynda Carter as Principal Powers.\nPage: Andrew Gunn (film producer). Sentence: He has worked with Walt Disney Pictures to produce movies such as \"Freaky Friday\" and \"Sky High\".",
